# Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF, on every
# platform.
#
# The scheduler vectors are regenerated by the CI and then compared with
# `git diff`. They were committed with CRLF, because the machine that
# wrote them runs Windows, while the CI writes them with LF -- so the
# comparison failed on the line endings alone and never on the
# scheduler. Marking the files as text makes git normalise both sides
# before comparing them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vectors and the schema are generated artefacts: they must not be
# touched by a merge driver.
android/app/src/test/resources/srs_vectors.json -diff
android/app/schemas/**/*.json -diff

# The Windows batch file needs CRLF: cmd.exe does not run a .bat file
# whose lines end with a bare LF.
android/gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
